 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the village of Skaneateles, county of Onondaga, to convey its interest in Austin Park to the town of Skaneateles",
    "basePrintNo": "S7500",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7500-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Onondaga County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7500\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act in relation to authorizing the village of\nSkaneateles, county of Onondaga, to convey its interest in Austin Park\nto the town of Skaneateles\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL :\n\nThis bill would authorize the Village of Skaneateles to convey its\ninterest in Austin Park to the Town of Skaneateles\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 - Authorizes the Village of Skaneateles to discontinue and\nalienate the lands known as \"Austin Park\" and to enter into a contract\nto convey its interest to the Town of Skaneateles. Any revenue\nreceived by the Village of Skaneateles from the transfer shall be used\nfor capital improvements .\n\nSection 2 - Legal Description of the lands.\n\nSection 3 - The parklands transferred and all structures and\nfacilities situated on such parklands shall be maintained, owned and\noperated by the Town of Skaneateles.\n\nSection 4 - Where the availability of such parklands and facilities\nare limited, the use of such parklands and facilities must be\ndetermined by an equitable method.\n\nSection 5 - Subject to the provisions and after completion of the\ntransfer, the Town of Skaneateles, acting through its town board, is\nauthorized to lease to a not-for-profit entity an unused portion of\nthe building known as the \"Austin Pavilion, for the purpose of\nproviding service to children.\n\nSection 6 - Any revenues received by the Town of Skaneateles in\nconnection with the lease shall be used for capital improvements of\nexisting park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 7 - Should the lease described in section five of this act be\nterminated, such property shall revert to the Town of Skaneateles for\npublic park and recreational purposes.\n\nSection 7 - Effective date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill would enable the Town of Skaneateles to acquire Austin Park\non Jordan and East Austin Streets. The town has leased this property\nfor several years and now seeks improvements to the property that the\nVillage does not have the resources to accomplish. Therefore, it has\nbeen deemed to be in the best interest of both localities for the Town\nto acquire this property from the Village.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
